  "query_preview": "../Wednesday through Friday/...\nWith the most impactful weather in the rear-view, winds across \nthe panhandle begin to diminish through Wednesday. Rain is likely \nto continue due to a series of fronts moving through the area, but\nwinds are expected to diminish to less than 20kts in the inner \nchannels, and less than 30kts in Lynn Canal, Clarence Strait, and \ncoastal Gulf waters. A series of about 3 or 4 fronts are expected \nto track across the panhandle from Wednesday through Saturday \nnight bringing light to moderate rain, but are expected to be \nseasonable. With low pressure moving through the gulf and high \npressure established over the Yukon and British Columbia, a \nstronger east/west gradient sets up across the panhandle. Winds \nare likely to be east to northeast in direction through much of \nthis time with east/west oriented channels likely to see \nchanneling of winds.",
